{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '97,135p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc; rg -n 'store|modules' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | head -35; rg -n 'self|resume-task' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '97,135p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc; rg -n 'store|modules' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | head -35; rg -n 'self|resume-task' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"\n(defn- unsatisfied!\n  ([] (unsatisfied! nil))\n  ([identity]\n   (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n            (cond-> {} (some? identity)\n                    (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity)))))\n\n\n(defn- undecodable!\n  [data]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable data))\n\n\n(defn- not-at-safepoint!\n  [pc]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint {:yin.k/pc pc}))\n\n\n(defn- outcome\n  \"The S7.9 data outcome exception `e` carries, or nil.\"\n  [e]\n  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n    (when (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d)))\n\n\n(defn- call!\n  \"Run `f`, answering its value, or the data outcome it refused with.\n   A throw with no outcome vocabulary is a defect, not a refusal: it\n   propagates.\"\n  [f]\n  (try (f)\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (if-let [d (outcome e)] d (throw e)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The one cell map (14.1.2 lift step 2): minted across the WHOLE set\n;; =============================================================================\n30:  {:modules {}, :effect-handlers {}})\n41:  \"Descend a registry's :modules map along path, a sequence of symbols.\n60:  \"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\n61:   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\"\n62:  [modules module-name]\n64:                     modules\n73:            (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n81:   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :cells\n84:   :stores :cells :images}`, the cells being the logical cursor cells its\n95:                 :stores (:stores lifted),\n110:    (vec (walk (:modules registry)))))\n118:  (walk-path (:modules registry) (symbol->path sym)))\n134:(defn list-modules\n137:  (keys (:modules registry)))\n141:;; Host modules\n220:      (assoc-in (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n231:                 :stores {}})))\n394:     `:modules` (the child's module view), `:origin`, and `:ancestry`.\")\n413:     captured values encoded by `encode`, with `:yin.k/store-of` when the\n420:     decoded by `decode`, carrying the marker's `:yin.k/store-of`. A\n432:     adds the store, the module stores, `:parked`, `:wait-set` and\n450:   writer the composition supplied. No store instruction reaches it.\"\n529:   did, naming the modules it has.\"\n537:      (some? (resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n552:                       :available (vec (list-modules (:modules state)))}))\n581:  \"A registry with the built-in effect handlers and no modules.\"\n18:   `resume-task` is the lower, and its reader is version-aware (M-next\n144:  \"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\n202:   table itself keys by -- so a sort comparison never mints a number\n267:  (let [self (volatile! nil)\n269:                (sort-by (comp @self keyfn) jing.cbor/encoded-compare coll))\n275:    (vreset! self encode)\n480:  \"The wire variant the observed entry itself carries, from its shape\n704:(declare export-task validate-body resume-task)\n719:   (14.1.1's :install row).  A child that cannot export itself refuses\n827:   pending close, or a cursorless `:link-request` entry -- itself or any\n882:             ;; the pending-child gap the walk cannot close itself: an\n1191:   the cell table itself, each frame's registers AND pending (the\n1287:        ;; at the one safepoint kind whose meaning is the park itself,\n1496:                     resumed (resume-task\n1682:(defn resume-task\n1693:   restoration itself.  `opts` may name `:exclusive` (a version-0 body\n1707:   (resume-task recv bytes attach! nil))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'clj -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v1-test'","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v1-test\n\nFAIL in (v1-grant-boundary-and-consistency) (handoff_v1_test.cljc:249)\n{:status :ok, :kind :blocked, :vm #yin.vm.semantic.SemanticVM{:blocked? true, :bridge nil, :halted? false, :k nil, :program nil, :control nil, :env {}, :stack [], :id-counter 2, :parked {}, :primitives {first #:yin.k{:profile :yin.k.pp/sha256-b700e05219855ce14f53129df01e28db7a3dbfcabfe43150fe93744065be112d, :class :pure, :arities [1], :effects #{}, :host-state :none, :function #object[clojure.core$first__5470 0x386aa805 \"clojure.core$first__5470@386aa805\"]}, = #:yin.k{:profile :yin.k.pp/sha256-c52d5f54db8beab950dcc4fdc544459df44ab734acd19580c1f81a98a57e49e4, :class :pure, :arities [0 1 2 :variadic], :effects #{}, :host-state :none, :function #object[clojure.core$_EQ_ 0x3cb034af \"clojure.core$_EQ_@3cb034af\"]}, < #:yin.k{:profile :yin.k.pp/sha256-0ad023fc63efcbca9c0fa42f5e570b80b3f89267d31a2a8b6b8f7392bbd59377, :class :pure, :arities [1 2 :variadic], :effects #{}, :host-state :none, :function #object[clojure.core$_LT_ 0x491cb3d0 \"clojure.core$_LT_@491cb3d0\"]}, rest #:yin.k{:profile :yin.k.pp/sha256-4533d640ff5be38560456acda68c2677cfe6fdbdcbce01f68e18088c3765859e, :class :pure, :arities [1], :effects #{}, :host-state :none, :function #object[yin.vm$fn__10216$fn__10219 0x4e91272d \"yin.vm$fn__10216$fn__10219@4e91272d\"]}, <= #:yin.k{:profile :yin.k.pp/sha256-0f44485d7ba94fefb79730ad777faee7b740ed60ae5a7f5c4602263e69344f9e, :class :pure, :arities [1 2 :variadic], :effects #{}, :host-state :none, :function #object[clojure.core$_LT__EQ_ 0x2356947a \"clojure.core$_LT__EQ_@2356947a\"]}, * #:yin.k{: